sdata> -- Regression guard for the same REPL dispatch trap note_repl_dispatch.cmd
sdata> -- exercises for NOTE (see ADR-059): before the fix, UNSET was missing from
sdata> -- Is_Immediate, so the REPL queued it as deferred instead of dispatching it
sdata> -- at once -- and since Stmt_UNSET was also never in Process_One_Record's
sdata> -- whitelist, it silently never fired at all interactively, under any usage
sdata> -- pattern. NEW /PROGRAM clears the still-queued SET X=1 first so this
sdata> -- matches batch's already-correct isolated-UNSET result.
sdata> NEW
sdata> USE MOCK
Generating mock data...
sdata> SET X = 1
sdata> RUN
RUN complete. 3 records and 3 variables processed.
sdata> NEW /PROGRAM
sdata> UNSET X
sdata> PRINT X
sdata> RUN
Error: undefined variable "X"
sdata> QUIT
